---
description: Keep tests meaningful, failures visible, and user-facing flows fully wired
alwaysApply: true
---

# Quality

- Test observable behavior, not private helpers or call counts alone.
- Cover the normal path, one important edge case, and the error path.
- Do not delete, weaken, or comment out a failing test to get green.
- Fail visibly with an actionable message; never replace a real error with fake success or empty data.
- Log the start and outcome of every external call without exposing secrets.
- Before delivery, confirm the feature is reachable through its real entry point and that dependencies, routes, handlers, and configuration are connected.
- Run the whole relevant suite before saying done.
